## Why This Is Asked
Tests a three-dimensional DP that models constrained path planning with a binary obstacle grid and a budget of unblocks. Requires careful state definition, transitions, and path reconstruction. 

## Key Concepts
- DP with an extra dimension for unblocks (t)
- Handling blocked vs unblocked cells in transitions
- Path reconstruction from 3D DP table
- Time/space trade-offs and rolling optimization

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPath(grid, blocked, k) {
  const n = grid.length, m = grid[0].length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array.from({length: m}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG)));
  if (!blocked[0][0]) dp[0][0][0] = grid[0][0];
  else if (k > 0) dp[0][0][1] = grid[0][0];
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j < m; j++) {
      for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
        const val = grid[i][j];
        if (i > 0) {
          dp[i][j][t] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t], dp[i-1][j][t] + val * (blocked[i][j] ? 0 : 1));
          if (blocked[i][j] && t > 0) dp[i][j][t] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t], dp[i-1][j][t-1] + val);
        }
        if (j > 0) {
          dp[i][j][t] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t], dp[i][j-1][t] + val * (blocked[i][j] ? 0 : 1));
          if (blocked[i][j] && t > 0) dp[i][j][t] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t], dp[i][j-1][t-1] + val);
        }
      }
    }
  }
  return dp[n-1][m-1][0];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you recover the actual path from the 3D DP and handle ties?
- What optimizations would you apply for large grids or memory constraints?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests comprehensive DP design for partitioning problems with nonlinear segment costs involving both min and sum operations, requiring careful handling of base cases and path reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-dimensional DP over partition indices
- Range minimum query optimization within transitions
- Complete solution from base cases through reconstruction
- Space-time tradeoffs and optimization strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Initialize DP table and parent pointers
dp[0][0] = 0;
for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
  dp[i][1] = rangeMin(1, i) * prefix[i];
  parent[i][1] = 0;
}

// Fill DP table
for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
  for (let i = t; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let p = t-1; p < i; p++) {
      const segVal = rangeMin(p+1, i) * (prefix[i] - prefix[p]);
      const total = dp[p][t-1] + segVal;
      if (total > dp[i][t]) {
        dp[i][t] = total;
        parent[i][t] = p;
      }
    }
  }
}

// Reconstruct segments
let i = n, t = k;
while (t > 0) {
  const p = parent[i][t];
  segments[t] = [p+1, i];
  i = p;
  t--;
}
```

